      tag: "CLIFFHANGER → CHAPTER 6",
      body: "Now you know which hours the market can move — and exactly why. But look at our map again, at the daily peak. It doesn't land on some exchange's opening bell. It lands at 8:30am in Washington — the minute a government agency publishes a single number.\n\nA number that's known in advance: the date, a year ahead; the hour, a month ahead; analysts' forecasts, a week ahead. Only the value itself is unknown. And the moment it's published, it instantly multiplies volatility several times over — measured at roughly 576 percent on the employment report.\n\nThink about what that means. The day's strongest move isn't made by a secret player or a clever scheme — it's made by a press release sitting in a public calendar you can look at right now. Everyone knows when. Nobody knows what. And an entire industry is built on exactly that gap.\n\nThe next episode is about how to read that calendar: why markets sometimes fall on good news, what \"buy the rumour, sell the fact\" actually means, and why a number that comes in exactly on forecast still moves the market.",
